<body>

<h1 class="main-title">Bank Interest Demonstration</h1>

<div class="meta-field"><span class="meta-label">Title:</span> Bank Interest Rate Demonstration using Dynamic Method Dispatch</div>

<div class="meta-field"><span class="meta-label">Objective/Aim:</span><br>
To demonstrate method overriding and runtime polymorphism in Java by calculating different rates of interest for different banks.</div>

<h2 class="section-header">System Requirements :</h2>
<div class="sub-heading">Hardware</div>
<ul>
<li>Standard PC/Laptop</li><li>Intel Core i3/i5 processor or equivalent</li><li>Minimum 4 GB RAM</li><li>Minimum 500 MB free storage</li><li>Keyboard and Monitor</li>
</ul>
<div class="sub-heading">Software</div>
<ul>
<li>Operating System: Windows/Linux/macOS</li><li>Java Development Kit (JDK 17 or JDK 21)</li>
<li>Text Editor or IDE such as Eclipse, IntelliJ IDEA, NetBeans, or VS Code</li><li>Command Prompt/Terminal</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section-header">Algorithm / Logic Description:</h2>
<ol>
<li>Create a base class named <code>Bank</code> with a method <code>interestRate()</code> returning the default interest rate (4.0).</li>
<li>Create subclasses <code>StateBank</code>, <code>ICICIBank</code>, and <code>PunjabBank</code> that extend <code>Bank</code>.</li>
<li>Override the <code>interestRate()</code> method in each derived class to return their respective rates: 7.0%, 6.5%, and 6.0%.</li>
<li>Create the <code>InterestDemo</code> class containing the <code>main()</code> method.</li>
<li>Prompt the user to enter the bank name using the <code>Scanner</code> class.</li>
<li>Declare a <code>Bank</code> reference variable and dynamically assign the corresponding subclass instance based on user input.</li>
<li>Call <code>interestRate()</code> through the superclass reference to demonstrate runtime polymorphism (Dynamic Method Dispatch).</li>
<li>Display the retrieved rate of interest and close the scanner.</li>
<li>Stop the program.</li>
</ol>

<div class="page-break"></div>

